WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.020
Happy Monday, welcome to Tesla Short's Time, daily, episode 483.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.180
It's May 25th, 2026, and I am Patrick and Vancouver.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.160
A new week, and plenty happening with Tesla.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.660
Franz von Holthausen confirmed the Tesla Roadster will be built at Gigafactory, Texas,

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.680
locking in the long delayed Halo cars manufacturing location.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:25.840
Franz von Holthausen revealed on the ride the Lightning podcast

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.440
that the next generation Roadster will be assembled at Gigafactory, Texas.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:36.500
The announcement clarifies a key piece of Tesla's future vehicle roadmap after years of speculation

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:42.720
about the car's status. Texas already handles Cybertruck and certain model Y variants,

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:46.900
giving the site experience with low volume, high performance builds.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:52.800
The choice also aligns with Tesla's pattern of concentrating new programs at its most advanced

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:58.780
factories. Observers will watch for any updates on supplier tooling or battery integration that

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.320
follow the reveal. Taking a step back from today's headlines,

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.420
the confirmation that the Roadster will be built at Gigafactory, Texas,

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:11.060
quietly challenges the assumption that Halo vehicles must be produced at low volume,

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:14.660
dedicated facilities to justify their price and complexity.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:19.620
The decision places a low volume, high performance car on the same lines,

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.960
already running Cybertruck and refreshed model Y output.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:29.760
That choice forces a tighter integration between the 4680 cell program, structural battery packs,

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.780
and the vehicle's extreme performance targets. It also means any yield or throughput gains achieved

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:41.200
for the Roadster will directly translate to higher volume programs, rather than remaining

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:47.540
isolated in a separate plant. If the Texas team can hit both the cost and performance numbers on

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:53.100
a shared line, the precedent could reshape how Tesla sequences future low volume models

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:59.720
and where it invests incremental capital. Now shifting to near-term software that owners can

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:07.120
use today. Tesla posted that owners can let FSD supervise to handle the driving on scenic road trips,

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:12.860
so passengers can focus on the landscape. The message positions the supervised system as a

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:18.840
practical tool for longer leisure drives rather than just commuting. It comes as Tesla continues

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:25.600
to expand FSD availability in new markets. The post links back to the company's drive experience

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:31.840
page. Next data point to watch is whether engagement metrics rise in tourist corridors this summer.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:37.940
Release notes and tester reports show dramatically reduced driver prompts on long Texas drives.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:44.840
One reviewer covered 41 miles over three days with zero interventions, prompting Musk to share

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:50.820
the feedback publicly. A new on-screen street counter now tracks miles since the last takeover.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:56.120
The build is described as the first truly refined version by multiple testers.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:03.100
April 2026 marked the first month the supervised fleet posted a rolling crash rate below the

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:11.400
NHTSA human average. Of 17 unredacted incidents, nine were other party fault and only three involve

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:17.240
the autonomous system at low speeds. Teller operator errors accounted for two at fault cases.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:24.020
While autonomy inches forward in the US, Europe is changing how owners pay for it. As of May

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:30.800
21, new purchases in the UK and Europe move to 99 euros per month recurring. The change converts

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:37.180
one time software sales into annual recurring revenue. Lithuania became the second EU country

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:43.800
to approve supervised FSD via mutual recognition of the Dutch certification. Greece is expected to

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:49.720
follow in June. Revenue model changes in Europe sit alongside lighter in-car features rolling out

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:55.160
everywhere. Tesla highlighted that owners can say hey, GROC to ask about geological features,

00:03:55.480 --> 00:04:00.320
local history, or nearby points of interest while traveling. The feature turns the voice

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:05.960
assistant into a real-time companion for exploration rather than only navigation or media control.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:10.260
It builds on GROC's existing integration in newer vehicles.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:16.340
The timing coincides with summer travel season messaging. Watch for any reported usage spikes

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:22.340
or feature expansions in the next software branch. Tesla posted a customer testimonial about

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:28.180
achieving a no car payment lifestyle through FSD use and linked to its drive experience page.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:34.600
The anecdote frames FSD as a way to offset ownership costs via ride sharing or efficiency.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:39.940
It follows Tesla's pattern of amplifying owner success stories on social channels.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:46.620
The post uses a simple smile emoji to keep the tone light. Future earnings calls may quantify

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:53.140
how many owners cite similar economics. While software adds daily utility, hardware programs keep

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:59.180
posting small visual updates. The Optimus account posted a brief video of the robot in motion.

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:04.860
The clip adds to the steady stream of visual updates Tesla has shared ahead of the planned late

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:10.920
June reveal window. Viewers noted incremental improvements in gate and hand movement compared

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:16.240
with earlier footage. The post continues Tesla's approach of releasing small pieces of progress

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:21.700
rather than waiting for a single polished demo. The next major data point remains the targeted

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:28.020
reveal timing. The Optimus account posted a simple wave and heart emoji. The light hearted message

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:32.900
keeps the robot's social presence active while hardware development continues at Fremont.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:40.040
Such posts maintain public interest between more technical updates. Be roll from a recent Model SX

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:45.020
delivery event briefly showed what appears to be the one million unit per year production line.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:51.360
Observers noted the setup looked further along than prior public statement suggested. Tesla has

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:57.080
posted data collection operator roles across roughly a dozen facilities. The reveal remains

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:03.940
targeted for late June to early July. Humanoid progress remains early stage. Older vehicles face

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:10.140
their own long term questions. A Tesla VP stated the company has not ruled out future updates or

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:16.080
continued production for the Model S and Model X. The comment comes after speculation that both

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:22.120
sedans might be phased out in favor of newer platforms. Current production remains low volume

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:27.720
and focused on the plaid variants. The statement keeps the models in the portfolio without committing

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:33.880
to specific timelines. Investors will look for any capacity signals in the next factory utilization

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:41.960
update. A 2016 Model S that stayed with its original owner until 2026 recently changed hands

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:48.040
at a notably low figure. The sale highlights how early high mileage examples are aging in the

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:53.440
used market. Battery health and remaining warranty coverage likely influenced the final price.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:59.140
The transaction underscores the long-term depreciation curve for first-generation vehicles.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:05.100
Watch for similar sales data to gauge residual values ahead of potential refreshed models.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:11.900
Portfolio decisions sit against broader market moves worth noting. A starling commercial air

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:17.740
during the Indianapolis 500 broadcast. The placement puts the satellite internet service in front

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:24.620
of a large live sports audience. Tesla and SpaceX have overlapping ownership and technology overlap,

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:30.280
making the ad relevant to Tesla owners who use in-car connectivity. It is one of the higher

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:36.200
profile consumer marketing moments for starling this year. Track weather similar cross-promotion

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:42.320
appears in other major events. A Tesla raw T-pole asked Tesla owners whether they would rather have

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:48.300
faster charging or longer range on their next vehicle. The question drew strong opinions on both

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:54.700
sides, reflecting real-world trade-offs owners face on road trips. Faster charging reduces dwell

00:07:54.700 --> 00:08:00.840
time at superchargers, while extra range cuts the number of stops. The debate often surfaces when

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:06.980
new battery or motor options are rumored. The results may inform how Tesla prioritizes feature pack

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:12.680
and thermal upgrades. Marketing and owner priorities sit alongside the weekly market wrap.

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:17.660
There is a challenge worth discussing. The analysis argues that near-term

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:23.740
robotaxi revenue projections rest on optimistic deployment timelines that current fundamentals

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:29.440
do not yet support. Unsupervised fleet counts have remained flat for more than two weeks,

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:34.340
and teleoperator interventions have already contributed to documented incidents.

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:40.580
Tesla's ability to convert supervised miles into a scalable, profitable service will determine

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:46.600
whether the narrative can overcome slower vehicle demand signals. The piece frames the gap between

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:52.080
promised autonomy economics and today's delivery and margin trends as the central tension for

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:58.500
investors. Before we go, keep an eye on whether unsupervised fleet counts move in the coming days

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:06.420
